$detach_audio — extract audio from video

SUMMARY
  Extracts the audio track from each videos[] file into sounds[].

SYNTAX
  $detach_audio
  $detach_audio(format='wav')
  $detach_audio(format='mp3')

INPUT
  videos[] — required; MP4 and other ffmpeg-readable video files

OUTPUT
  sounds[] — one audio file per input video (videos[] cleared)

ARGUMENTS
  format= — wav (default, 44.1 kHz stereo PCM) | aac | mp3 | copy
            (copy keeps source codec; extension .m4a for aac/copy)

DEPENDENCIES
  ffmpeg + ffprobe: uv run python tools/download_ffmpeg.py  (→ tools/ffmpeg/)
  or system install on PATH

ENVIRONMENT
  AH_EMULATE_DETACH_AUDIO=1 — write stub sound links without ffmpeg

EXAMPLE
  @wav: $file('clip.mp4') -> $detach_audio -> $save('clip.wav')

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  No — output is sounds[] only (videos[] cleared).
